{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit cap (AB 12)","requirement":"A landlord may charge no more than one month's rent as a security deposit; landlords owning only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total may charge up to two months' rent.","key_value":"1 month's rent; 2 months' rent for small landlords","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental units generally; special allowance for owners of two rental properties with no more than four residential units total held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC of natural persons.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Small-landlord allowance: 2 rental properties, max 4 residential units total"},"exemptions":"Landlords owning only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total (natural person, family trust, or LLC whose members are natural persons) may charge up to two months' rent.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","citation":"AB 12","quoted_span":"Starting July 1, 2024, many landlords may only charge one month's rent for unfurnished and furnished units","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return deadline and itemization","requirement":"A landlord must return the deposit or any remaining portion within 21 days after the tenant leaves the unit vacant and, if deducting, give a written itemized statement with copies of bills, invoices, or receipts for repairs or cleaning.","key_value":"21 days","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies; deductions allowed only for rent default, tenant-caused damage beyond normal wear and tear, cleaning to the original level of cleanliness, and restoring or replacing property or furniture if the lease allows.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Board, Security Deposits page","quoted_span":"All or any remaining portion of a security deposit must be returned within 21 days after the tenant/s leave the unit vacant.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit interest under the Berkeley Rent Ordinance","requirement":"For units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, a landlord must pay the tenant interest on the security deposit at the end of each year, and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","key_value":"annual interest, prorated on move-out","coverage_conditions":"Tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance","quoted_span":"For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Move-out walk-through inspection offer","requirement":"Under state law, a landlord must offer a walk-through inspection during the last two weeks of the tenancy so the tenant can identify items needing repair or cleaning and correct them to avoid deposit deductions.","key_value":"last two weeks of tenancy","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies covered by state security deposit law.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Board, Security Deposits page","quoted_span":"Under state law, landlords must offer a walk-through inspection during the last two weeks of a tenancy to identify any items that need repair/cleaning.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Photograph of unit at start of new tenancy","requirement":"For tenancies beginning on or after July 1, 2025, a landlord must photograph the unit immediately before or at the start of the new tenancy to document its condition.","key_value":"photograph required at start of tenancy","coverage_conditions":"Tenancies that begin on or after July 1, 2025.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Tenancies beginning on or after July 1, 2025"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-07-01","citation":"Berkeley Rent Board, Security Deposits page","quoted_span":"For tenancies that begin on or after July 1, 2025, a landlord must photograph the unit immediately before or at the start of a new tenancy to document the condition of the unit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
